{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486104145,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk0NzYzMTEwOA=="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1486160901,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NzM3OTk1NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1250#issuecomment-277379955"},"message":"As we briefly chatted about I will first document briefly currently available approach and then we will go from there. Meanwhile, for http://wiki.cnbc.cmu.edu/Face_Place what I did to add it to our distribution was (redoing somewhat so might be typos)\n```shell\ncd labs\ndatalad create --no-annex -d . tarr\ncd tarr\ndatalad create -d . face_place\ncd face_place\n# here I cheated and copied working .datalad/crawl/crawl.cfg, but should work:\ndatalad crawl-init --template simple_with_archives url=http://wiki.cnbc.cmu.edu/Face_Place 'a_href_match_=.*\\.zip' tarballs=True leading_dirs_depth=0\n# this one should not be needed, should add/save automagically\ndatalad add --to-git .datalad/crawl/crawl.cfg \ndatalad crawl\n```\nand then I had some fun creating basic dataset descriptors and running into some imho odd save behaviours: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1254 ... then a few rounds of aggregate-metadata (seems it would be useful to have -S switch there too!, see also now #1255), and all what is needed atm to get it finally published to our datasets.datalad.org -- from the top directory:\n1. \nSince there is no --since handling AFAIK, just need this way ATM, used new API for create-sibling (`-s` option):\n```shell\n datalad --dbg create-sibling --shared all --existing=skip -r -s datalad-public ssh://datasets.datalad.org/srv/datasets.datalad.org/www/\n...\n[INFO   ] Connecting ... \n[INFO   ] Creating target dataset /mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/labs/tarr at /srv/datasets.datalad.org/www/labs/tarr \n[INFO   ] Creating target dataset /mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/openfmri/ds000214 at /srv/datasets.datalad.org/www/openfmri/ds000214 \n[INFO   ] Creating target dataset /mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/labs/tarr/face_place at /srv/datasets.datalad.org/www/labs/tarr/face_place \n```\nwhich took a while (was subject to double sensing, #1255), flooded my screen with \"[INFO   ] Skipping datasets with an already configured sibling 'datalad-public': ...\" listing all those now many datasets, BUT seems have been doing the right thing (created also a dataset for openfmri/ds000214  as well which I might have not had)\n2.\nSince #1237 is not yet finished/merged, I had to \n```shell\ngit submodule foreach --recursive bash -c \"git config --get remote.datalad-public.push | grep -q 'heads/\\*' || {  git config --add remote.datalad-public.push 'refs/tags/*'; git config --add remote.datalad-public.push 'refs/heads/*'; }\"\n```\nfor a check I did \n```shell\n$\u003e cat labs/tarr/face_place/.git/config \n[core]\n\trepositoryformatversion = 0\n\tfilemode = true\n\tbare = false\n\tlogallrefupdates = true\n[annex]\n\tuuid = f189041e-bdbf-488a-961a-ea7b6dcec86b\n\tversion = 5\n\tbackends = MD5E\n[remote \"datalad-archives\"]\n\tannex-externaltype = datalad-archives\n\tannex-uuid = 64841f3b-650b-4489-856e-aff3c6286af3\n\tannex-cost = 500.0\n\tannex-availability = LocallyAvailable\n[remote \"datalad-public\"]\n\tpush = refs/tags/*\n\tpush = refs/heads/*\n```\nto realize in a surprise that `create-sibling` **did not register that as a remote to the original dataset!**  I wonder why I was even given a name?!  I think it was registering them before just fine :-(  so now I had to add those remotes manually.\n3. publish!  I thought it would be a piece of cake since there is a good `--since` BUT I was surprised to see\n```shell\n(git)smaug:/mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl[master]git\n$\u003e datalad publish --to=datalad-public -r\nNothing was published\n```\nwhich is really sad since\n```shell\n$\u003e git lg datalad-public/master..master \n* 624430e - (HEAD -\u003e master) [DATALAD] aggregated meta data (24 minutes ago) [Yaroslav Halchenko]\n* ae4afa5 - [DATALAD] auto-saved changes (26 minutes ago) [Yaroslav Halchenko]\n* 7a4bd3a - fixed up json (34 minutes ago) [Yaroslav Halchenko]\n* 3b37735 - [DATALAD] aggregated meta data (7 days ago) [Yaroslav Halchenko]\n* 4a9e730 - [DATALAD] auto-saved changes (7 days ago) [Yaroslav Halchenko]\n```\nand so `--since` should have done correct detection as it did before (I think)... and indeed probably since now is handled only if explicitly specified.  So I deactivated virtualenv and went back to released 0.4.1, and it did the right thing:\n```shell\n$\u003e datalad publish --to=datalad-public -r\n[INFO   ] Publishing \u003cDataset path=/mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/labs/haxby/raiders\u003e to datalad-public \n[INFO   ] 3bf7193..07861d6\n|  \n[INFO   ] f5d4b54..df51dc4\n|  \n[INFO   ] Publishing \u003cDataset path=/mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/labs/haxby\u003e to datalad-public \n[INFO   ] c88cc54..f0f80c2\n|  \n[INFO   ] Publishing \u003cDataset path=/mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/labs/mitchell/science2008\u003e to datalad-public \n[INFO   ] a1bb300..514aa4a\n...\n```\nuntil it failed since I forgot to manually configure remote now in that openfmri dataset :-/  heh -- so would need to fix for that manually and rerun with explicit --since.  (now reported in #1256)\n\nSo overall to me -- crawling is not a problem, publishing remains a hurdle... I will try with #1237 as soon as I should I guess","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486387299,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk1MDI3Nzg2NA=="},"added":["TERRIFIC!"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1494855261,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEwODIyNTEyNDE="},"added":["good first issue"],"removed":[]},{"t